1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,030
Welcome to the Fiddy Working Heritage Farm.

2
00:00:05,030 --> 00:00:08,775
This open-air museum gives you the experience of agriculture

3
00:00:08,775 --> 00:00:14,600
and rural life in the English countryside at the end of the nineteenth century.

4
00:00:14,600 --> 00:00:19,520
So you'll see a typical farm of that period, and like me

5
00:00:19,680 --> 00:00:22,650
all the staff are dressed in clothes of that time.

6
00:00:22,650 --> 00:00:28,210
I must give you some advice and safety tips before we go any further.

7
00:00:28,210 --> 00:00:33,650
As it's a working farm, please don't frighten or injure the animals.

8
00:00:33,650 --> 00:00:38,750
We have a lot here, and many of them are breeds that are now quite rare.

9
00:00:38,750 --> 00:00:42,819
And do stay at a safe distance from the tools:

10
00:00:42,819 --> 00:00:47,380
some of them have sharp points which can be pretty dangerous

11
00:00:47,520 --> 00:00:49,330
so please don't touch them.

12
00:00:49,330 --> 00:00:51,610
We don't want any accidents, do we?

13
00:00:51,610 --> 00:00:57,187
The ground is very uneven, and you might slip if you're wearing sandals

14
00:00:57,187 --> 00:01:04,050
so I'm glad to see you're all wearing shoes we always advise people to do that.

15
00:01:04,050 --> 00:01:07,911
Now, children of all ages are very welcome here,

16
00:01:07,911 --> 00:01:13,360
and usually even very young children love the ducks and lambs

17
00:01:13,360 --> 00:01:16,490
so do bring them along next time you come.

18
00:01:16,490 --> 00:01:20,531
I don't think any of you have brought dogs with you,

19
00:01:20,531 --> 00:01:22,460
but in case you have

20
00:01:22,460 --> 00:01:27,510
I'm afraid they'll have to stay in the car park, unless they're guide dogs.

21
00:01:27,510 --> 00:01:33,130
I'm sure you'll understand that they could cause a lot of problems on a farm.

22
00:01:33,130 --> 00:01:42,040
Now let me give you some idea of the layout of the farm.

23
00:01:42,040 --> 00:01:47,393
The building where you bought your tickets is the New Barn, immediately to your right,

24
00:01:47,393 --> 00:01:52,300
and we're now at the beginning of the main path to the farmland

25
00:01:52,300 --> 00:01:55,600
and of course the car park is on your left.

26
00:01:55,600 --> 00:02:02,240
The scarecrow you can see in the car park in the corner beside the main path,

27
00:02:02,240 --> 00:02:06,220
is a traditional figure for keeping the birds away from crops

28
00:02:06,220 --> 00:02:09,710
but our scarecrow is a permanent sculpture.

29
00:02:09,710 --> 00:02:15,200
It's taller than a human being, so you can see it from quite a distance.

30
00:02:15,200 --> 00:02:19,650
If you look ahead of you, you'll see a maze.

31
00:02:19,650 --> 00:02:22,000
It's opposite the New Barn

32
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:26,900
beside the side path that branches off to the right just over there.

33
00:02:26,900 --> 00:02:30,320
The maze is made out of hedges

34
00:02:30,320 --> 00:02:33,417
which are too tall for young children to see over them,

35
00:02:33,417 --> 00:02:37,400
but it's quite small, so you can't get lost in it!

36
00:02:37,400 --> 00:02:43,900
Now, can you see the bridge crossing the fish pool further up the main path?

37
00:02:43,900 --> 00:02:50,850
If you want to go to the cafe, go towards the bridge and turn right just before it.

38
00:02:50,850 --> 00:02:56,750
Walk along the side path and the cafe's on the first bend you come to.

39
00:02:56,750 --> 00:03:03,230
The building was originally the schoolhouse, and it's well over a hundred years old.

40
00:03:03,230 --> 00:03:08,133
As you may know, we run skills workshops here,

41
00:03:08,133 --> 00:03:13,580
where you can learn traditional crafts like woodwork and basket-making.

42
00:03:13,580 --> 00:03:16,540
You can see examples of the work

43
00:03:16,540 --> 00:03:20,740
and talk to someone about the courses, in the Black Barn.

44
00:03:20,740 --> 00:03:24,180
If you take the side path to the right,

45
00:03:24,180 --> 00:03:26,660
here, just by the New Barn

46
00:03:26,720 --> 00:03:31,060
you'll come to the Black Barn just where the path first bends.

47
00:03:31,060 --> 00:03:35,460
Now I mustn't forget to tell you about picnicking

48
00:03:35,700 --> 00:03:39,150
as I can see some of you have brought your lunch with you.

49
00:03:39,150 --> 00:03:44,720
You can picnic in the field, though do clear up behind you, of course.

50
00:03:44,720 --> 00:03:49,862
Or if you'd prefer a covered picnic area, there's one near the farmyard:

51
00:03:49,862 --> 00:03:55,400
just after you cross the bridge, there's a covered picnic spot on the right.

52
00:03:55,400 --> 00:04:00,370
And the last thing to mention is Fiddy House itself.

53
00:04:00,370 --> 00:04:03,260
From here you can cross the bridge

54
00:04:03,260 --> 00:04:08,040
then walk along the footpath through the field to the left of the farmyard.

55
00:04:08,040 --> 00:04:13,060
That goes to the house, and it'll give you a lovely view of it.

56
00:04:13,060 --> 00:04:16,060
It's certainly worth a few photographs

57
00:04:16,420 --> 00:04:20,630
but as it's a private home, I'm afraid you can't go inside.

58
00:04:20,630 --> 00:04:27,270
Right. Well, if you're all ready, well set off on our tour of the farm.
